<body class="bg-gray-100 font-sans">
  <%- include('partial/header') %>
  </h1>
  <main class="container mx-auto bg-white shadow-lg rounded-lg p-8 mt-10 max-w-xl">
    <h2 class="text-2xl text-gray-800 font-bold text-center mb-6">Engineering Physics</h2>
    <h1 class="text-2xl">Unit 1.0:Frame of Reference and Oscillations</h1>
    <p>Non-Inertial frame of refrence</p>
    <p>Rotating coordinate system</p>
    <p>Centripetal and Coriolis acceleration and its application in weather system</p>
    <p>Harmonic Oscillator</p>
    <p>Damped Harmonic motion: overdamped, critically Damped and light damped oscillators</p>
    <p>Force Oscillators and Resonance</p>
    <h1 class="text-2xl">Unit 2.0:Optics and LASER</h1>
    <p>Huygens's Principal</p>
    <p>Superposition of Waves and interference of Light by wave font-splitting and amplitude-splitting</p>
    <p>Young's double slit experiment</p>
    <p>Michelson interferometer</p>
    <p>Fraunhofer diffraction from singlr slit and circular aperture</p>
    <p>Diffraction Grating and their resolving power</p>
    <p>Einstein's theory of matter-radiations interaction</p>
    <p>Einstein's Coefficients(A and B)</p>
    <p>Amplification by population inversion</p>
    <p>Different type of lasers-Gas Laser,Helium-Neon Laser, Solid State Laser(Ruby,Neodyminm), Semiconductor Laser</p>
    <h1 class="text-2xl">Unit 3.0:Quantum Mechanics</h1>
    <p>Compton Effect</p>
    <p>Photoelectric Effect</p>
    <p>Wave Partical duality</p>
    <p>de Broglie's hypothesis</p>
    <p>Heisenberg's Uncertainty Principal</p>
    <p>Wave function and wave packets</p>
    <p>Phase and group velocities</p>
    <p>Schrodinger's Wave Equation</p>
    <p>Normalization</p>
    <p>Expectation values</p>
    <p>Eigenvalues and Eigenfunction</p>
    <p>Application of Schrodinger Wave Equation for partical in one dimensional box: its wavefunction and eigenvalue of energy and momentum</p>
    <h1 class="text-2xl">Unit 4.0:Vector Calculus and Electrostatics</h1>
    <p>Gradient, Divergence and Curl</p>
    <p>Line, Surface and Volume integrals</p>
    <p>Gauss's Divergence theorem and Stokes' theorem in Cartesian Coordinate</p>
    <p>Gauss's Law and its applications</p>
    <p>Divergence and Curl of Electrostatic field</p>
    <p>Electrostatics Potential</p>
    <p>Boundary Conditions</p>
    <p>Poisson's and Laplace's equations</p>
    <p>Dielectics</p>
    <p>Polarization</p>
    <p>Bound Charges</p>
    <p>Electric displacement</p>
    <p>Boundary Condition in dielectrics</p>
    <h1 class="text-2xl">Unit 5.0:Magnetostatics and Electrodynamics</h1>
    <p>Lorentz force</p>
    <p>Biot-savart and Ampere's circuital laws and their applications</p>
    <p>Divergence and Curl of Magneto static fields</p>
    <p>Magnetic vector potential</p>
    <p>Force and torque on a magnetic diople</p>
    <p>Magnetic Materials</p>
    <p>Magnetization</p>
    <p>Bound currents</p>
    <p>Boundary conditions</p>
    <p>Ohm's law</p>
    <p>Motional EMF</p>
    <p>Faraday's Law</p>
    <p>Lenz's law</p>
    <p>Self and mutual inductance</p>
    <p>Energy stored in magnetic field</p>
    <p>Maxwell's equations in vacuum and nonconducting medium</p>
    <p>Continuity Equation</p>
    <p>Poynting theorem</p>
    <p>Wave Equation: plain electromagnetic wave in vacuum and their transverse nature and Polarization</p>
    <h1 class="text-2xl">Unit 6.0:Solids and Semi-Conductors</h1>
    <p>Free electron theory of metal</p>
    <p>Fermi level</p>
    <p>Bloch's theorem for particle and origin of energy band</p>
    <p>Kroning-Penney modal and origin of energy band</p>
    <p>Metals,semiconductors and insulators</p>
    <p>Intrinsic and extrinsic semiconcuctors</p>
    <p>Carrier transport, diffusion and drift</p>
    <p>P-N junction</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl text-gray-800 font-bold text-center mb-6">Text/Reference Books</h2>
    <h1>1. Quantum Physics of Atoms, Molecules, Solids, Nuclei and Particles, R. Eisberg R. Resnick, Wiley India Pvt. Ltd ISBN 978-81-265-0818-1</h1>
    <h1>2. Theory of Vibration with Application, W.T. Thomson M.D. Dahleh, Pearson India ISBN 978-81-317-0482-0</h1>
    <h1>3. Introduction to Electrodynamics, D.J. Griffiths, Pearson India, ISBN 978-93-325-5044-5</h1>
    <h1>4. Optics, Ajay Ghatak, McGraw hill ISBN 978-93-901-1359-0</h1>
  </main>
</body>
